/* ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   mls-grade-7.js — what Missouri expects of a 7th grader, and where this
   year's plan meets it.

   🚨 THE STANDARDS ARE COPIED, NOT DERIVED. They come from DESE's 2016
   board-approved sets, the Excel exports at dese.mo.gov/media/file/, which are
   clean where the accessible PDFs extract as doubled characters. Codes and
   wording are verbatim. Do not reword them to read better.

   🚨 `status` AND `where` ARE A HUMAN JUDGEMENT, made once, by hand, against
   year-plan.js on 2026-09-21. Keyword matching was tried and rejected: it
   produces confident nonsense. When a course file changes, these do NOT move
   with it, so re-check the affected subject by hand and say so here.

     covered  the year plan teaches it
     partial  the idea is met, but not by name, or met in a different subject
     gap      nothing in the year plan touches it

   ⚠️ THIS IS A GAP-SPOTTING TOOL, NOT A SYLLABUS. Missouri homeschool law is
   hours based, 1,000 a year with 600 core, and there is no state test. A gap
   row is a difference, not a debt.

   ⚠️ TWO OF THE FOUR ARE NOT WRITTEN PER GRADE:
     · Science is one 6-8 band covering three years. Only the life science
       strand is scored here, because this is the life science year. LS3,
       heredity, is not in the band at all - Missouri puts it in 1, 3 and 9-12.
     · Social studies is written per COURSE, not per grade. World History is
       this year; American History is grade 8; Geography is neither.
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
